---
// src/pages/docs/protocol.astro
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const codecExample = `
import { encodeFrame, decodeFrame } from '@ajaymyth/core';

// Create a Protocol v2 frame with priority and custom routing key
const binaryFrame = encodeFrame({
  version: 2,                        // Protocol v2
  type: 0x09,                        // ROUTE_REQUEST
  priority: 6,                       // High priority queue (0-7)
  seq: 104,                          // Sequence No
  routingKey: 'sensors.temperature', // Custom string routing key (0-255 bytes)
  payload: Buffer.from('Hello AfterLink v2!')
});

console.log(binaryFrame); 

// Decoding on socket receipt
const decoded = decodeFrame(binaryFrame);
console.log(decoded.version);     // 2
console.log(decoded.priority);    // 6
console.log(decoded.routingKey);  // 'sensors.temperature'
console.log(decoded.payload.toString()); // Hello AfterLink v2!
`;
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="Binary Protocol v2 Specification" 
  description="Deep dive into AfterLink Protocol v2's 16-byte fixed binary frame format, priority queues (0-7), version negotiation, custom string routing keys, and frame types."
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "TechArticle",
    "headline": "Binary Protocol v2 Specification",
    "description": "Deep dive into AfterLink Protocol v2's 16-byte fixed binary frame format, priority queues (0-7), version negotiation, custom string routing keys, and frame types.",
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Javali Ajayakumar" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AfterLink" },
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://afterlink-docs.vercel.app/docs/protocol"
  }}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-al-border/50 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-al-white mb-2">Binary Frame Specification (Protocol v2)</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-al-muted leading-relaxed">
        AfterLink v2.0.2 operates on Protocol v2. Every packet consists of a rigid <strong>16-byte fixed header</strong>, followed by an optional variable-length UTF-8 routing key (0–255 bytes) and a MessagePack-encoded payload body.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Frame layout visualization grid -->
    <h2 id="byte-layout" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-8 mb-3 select-none">Header Byte Layout Mapping</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-al-muted leading-relaxed select-all mb-4">
      Below is the logical arrangement of AfterLink Protocol v2's 16-byte fixed header and payload layout on the TCP network wire:
    </p>

    <!-- Visual header grid -->
    <div class="bg-al-card border border-al-border rounded-xl p-6 mb-10 overflow-x-auto select-all shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-mono uppercase tracking-widest mb-4 select-none">
        Protocol v2 Frame Layout (16-Byte Fixed Header + Optional Routing Key + Payload)
      </p>
      <div class="font-mono text-xs min-w-[750px] select-all">
        <div class="flex mb-1">
          <!-- Magic Segment -->
          <div class="w-20 text-center text-al-cyan border border-al-cyan/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-al-cyan/5">
            Magic<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">2B (0xAF1C)</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Version Segment -->
          <div class="w-16 text-center text-al-green border border-al-green/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-al-green/5">
            Version<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">1B (0x02)</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Type Segment -->
          <div class="w-16 text-center text-yellow-500 border border-yellow-500/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-yellow-500/5">
            Type<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">1B</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Priority Segment -->
          <div class="w-16 text-center text-red-400 border border-red-400/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-red-400/5">
            Priority<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">1B (0-7)</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Flags Segment -->
          <div class="w-14 text-center text-blue-400 border border-blue-400/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-blue-400/5">
            Flags<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">1B</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Sequence Number Segment -->
          <div class="w-20 text-center text-purple-400 border border-purple-400/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-purple-400/5">
            Seq No.<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">2B (u16)</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Route Len Segment -->
          <div class="w-16 text-center text-pink-400 border border-pink-400/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-pink-400/5">
            Route Len<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">1B (0-255)</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Reserved Segment -->
          <div class="w-16 text-center text-gray-400 border border-gray-400/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-gray-400/5">
            Reserved<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">3B</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Payload Length Segment -->
          <div class="w-24 text-center text-orange-400 border border-orange-400/30 rounded px-1.5 py-3 mx-0.5 bg-orange-400/5">
            Payload Len<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-al-muted font-bold font-sans">4B (u32)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex mt-1.5">
          <!-- Routing Key Segment -->
          <div class="w-1/3 text-center text-pink-300 border border-dashed border-pink-500/40 rounded px-2 py-2.5 mx-0.5 bg-pink-500/5">
            Routing Key String<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-sans">0–255 Bytes (UTF-8)</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Variable Payload Segment -->
          <div class="flex-1 text-center text-al-muted border border-dashed border-al-border rounded px-2 py-2.5 mx-0.5 bg-al-bg/30">
            Payload Body Data<br/>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-sans">Variable size (MessagePack bytes)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Field Definitions Table -->
    <h2 id="field-reference" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-10 mb-3 select-none">Field Definitions</h2>
    
    <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6 border border-al-border rounded-lg bg-al-dark/20 select-all">
      <table class="w-full text-left font-mono text-xs divide-y divide-al-border select-all">
        <thead class="bg-al-card text-al-cyan select-none">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3">Field</th>
            <th class="p-3">Size</th>
            <th class="p-3">Wire Type</th>
            <th class="p-3">Offset (Bytes)</th>
            <th class="p-3">Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-al-border tabular-nums text-al-text select-all">
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-al-cyan">magic</td>
            <td class="p-3">2 bytes</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8[2]</td>
            <td class="p-3">0 – 1</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Protocol identifier: fixed <code>0xAF 0x1C</code>. Restricts incoming socket streams.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-al-green">version</td>
            <td class="p-3">1 byte</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8</td>
            <td class="p-3">2</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Protocol version encoder flag (<code>0x02</code> in v2; supports v1/v2 negotiation).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-yellow-500">type</td>
            <td class="p-3">1 byte</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8</td>
            <td class="p-3">3</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Message type byte determining how the frame is routed.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-red-400">priority</td>
            <td class="p-3">1 byte</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8</td>
            <td class="p-3">4</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Priority queue level (<code>0</code> = lowest/default, <code>7</code> = highest urgent priority).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-400">flags</td>
            <td class="p-3">1 byte</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8</td>
            <td class="p-3">5</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Control flags byte (compression, encryption, custom frame options).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-purple-400">seq</td>
            <td class="p-3">2 bytes</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt16BE</td>
            <td class="p-3">6 – 7</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Sequence index for reliable RPC matching. Wraps at <code>65535</code>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-pink-400">route_len</td>
            <td class="p-3">1 byte</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8</td>
            <td class="p-3">8</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Length of custom string routing key in bytes (0 to 255).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-400">reserved</td>
            <td class="p-3">3 bytes</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt8[3]</td>
            <td class="p-3">9 – 11</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Reserved padding bytes for 16-byte fixed header alignment and future extensions.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-orange-400">length</td>
            <td class="p-3">4 bytes</td>
            <td class="p-3">UInt32BE</td>
            <td class="p-3">12 – 15</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Big-endian size count of payload data in bytes (max ~4.29 GB).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-pink-300">routing_key</td>
            <td class="p-3">0–255 bytes</td>
            <td class="p-3">String</td>
            <td class="p-3">16 .. (16 + route_len)</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Optional UTF-8 custom string routing key for topic matching and RPC endpoints.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-al-muted">payload</td>
            <td class="p-3">variable</td>
            <td class="p-3">Buffer</td>
            <td class="p-3">(16 + route_len)+</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">MessagePack-encoded message body containing payload values.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Message Types Table -->
    <h2 id="message-types" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-12 mb-3 select-none">Message Types</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-al-muted leading-relaxed select-all">
      The Message Type flag byte defines the routing channel behavior of the server:
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6 border border-al-border rounded-lg bg-al-dark/20 select-all">
      <table class="w-full text-left font-mono text-xs divide-y divide-al-border select-all">
        <thead class="bg-al-card text-al-cyan select-none">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3">Hex Value</th>
            <th class="p-3">Constant</th>
            <th class="p-3">Direction</th>
            <th class="p-3">Purpose & Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-al-border tabular-nums text-al-text select-all">
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x01</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_REQUEST</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-green">Client &rarr; Server</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">RPC request — expects a responsive matching reply frame.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x02</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_RESPONSE</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-yellow-500">Server &rarr; Client</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">RPC response payload frame matched by sequence number.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x03</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_PUBLISH</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-green">Client &rarr; Server</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Broadcast a message frame to a Pub/Sub channel.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x04</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_SUBSCRIBE</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-green">Client &rarr; Server</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Subscribe to Pub/Sub channel notifications.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x05</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_BROADCAST</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-yellow-500">Server &rarr; Client</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Fan-out pub/sub message forwarded to active subscribers.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x06</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_STREAM</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-yellow-500">Server &rarr; Client</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Streaming data chunks (multi-frame chunk payloads).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x07</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_STREAM_END</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-yellow-500">Server &rarr; Client</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">End of stream signal payload packet.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0x08</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_ERROR</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-muted">Both</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Error flag indicating payload parsing or connection errors.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors bg-al-card/20">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-al-cyan">0x09</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan font-bold">ROUTE_REQUEST</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-green">Client &rarr; Server</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Dynamic topic & string routing key registration/lookup request (Protocol v2).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors bg-al-card/20">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-al-cyan">0x0A</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan font-bold">PRIORITY_ACK</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-muted">Both</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Priority-aware sequence acknowledgement frame (Protocol v2).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0xFE</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_ACK</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-muted">Both</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Acknowledge code payload packet matched by sequence number.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-al-card/30 transition-colors">
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">0xFF</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-cyan">MSG_PING</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-al-muted">Both</td>
            <td class="p-3 select-all">Keepalive heartbeat ping to check connection availability.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Protocol v2 Features -->
    <h2 id="version-negotiation" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-12 mb-3 select-none">Version Negotiation (v1 / v2)</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-al-muted leading-relaxed select-all">
      Protocol v2 introduces bidirectional version negotiation during the initial connection handshake. When an AfterLink v2 client connects, it advertises support for version <code>0x02</code>. If the target server is a legacy v1 endpoint, the client seamlessly falls back to the 10-byte header format.
    </p>

    <h2 id="priority-queues" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-10 mb-3 select-none">Priority Queues (Levels 0–7)</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-al-muted leading-relaxed select-all">
      Every Protocol v2 frame includes a 1-byte priority field supporting 8 queue levels (<code>0</code> to <code>7</code>):
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-al-muted select-all my-3">
      <li><strong>0–2 (Low / Bulk):</strong> Background sync, bulk streaming, and non-critical metrics.</li>
      <li><strong>3–5 (Normal):</strong> Default priority level for standard RPC requests and Pub/Sub broadcasts.</li>
      <li><strong>6–7 (Urgent / Control):</strong> High-priority control frames (such as <code>PRIORITY_ACK</code> and heartbeats) that jump execution queues ahead of lower-priority messages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="custom-routing-keys" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-10 mb-3 select-none">Custom String Routing Keys (0–255 Bytes)</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-al-muted leading-relaxed select-all">
      Protocol v2 allows embedding an inline UTF-8 string routing key directly in the frame header (controlled by <code>route_len</code>). This enables zero-deserialization routing: servers inspect the header's routing key to route frames instantly without decoding the MessagePack payload.
    </p>

    <!-- Low-Level Codec Code Example -->
    <h2 id="codec-example" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-al-white mt-12 mb-3 select-none">Low-Level Codec Code Example</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-al-muted leading-relaxed select-all">
      Using the <code>@ajaymyth/core</code> library, developers can encode and decode raw Protocol v2 frames directly on top of socket streams:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock code={codecExample} lang="javascript" filename="codec.js" />

